{{!-- HOMEFRONT MOVES — its own tab, reached from the rail. It used to be a permanently
      visible sidebar down the right of every steading tab; the icon rail took that edge, and
      a page gives the moves room to sit two-up instead of wrapping in a narrow column.

      The Roll Modifier is not here, in any shape. It came across with the moves as a segmented
      pill in the heading below, and before that it was a section of its own with a stacked
      radio list; both were STICKY, which meant a player who rolled one move with Advantage
      rolled the next four with it too and nobody noticed. Rolling a homefront move now asks,
      per roll, in a window that always starts at Normal — see module/dialogs/RollDialog.js.

      `.steading-moves-tab` stays on an INNER wrapper rather than on the panel itself. It
      carries `display: flex`, and an unlayered `display` on a `.tab` beats core's layered
      `.tab { display: none }` — the panel would then show on every tab at once, the trap
      documented on `.tab.stonetop-invocations` and the Notes tabs. Off the panel, this tab's
      show/hide is Foundry's alone, exactly like Overview and Residents.

      The moves themselves are the character sheet's move CARDS, not the compact one-line rows
      they were as a sidebar. Same `.stonetop-move-group` > `.items-list` > `.stonetop-item`
      shape, so they inherit the bordered card, the underlined title row and the masonry
      columns from `.tab.moves` — this panel is a `.tab.moves` too. The text a card shows was
      the hover panel's whole job, so that panel is gone from this sheet.

      The moves keep their wrapper even though they are now the tab's only section: the fold
      walk (a heading claims every FOLLOWING SIBLING until the next heading) has no other
      boundary, so a section added here later would be swallowed by this one's caret. --}}
<div class="tab moves" data-group="primary" data-tab="moves">
	<section class="sheet-tab steading-moves-tab">

	<div class="stonetop-move-group">
		{{!-- The h3 is written out rather than taken from `stonetop.section-heading` because
		      this heading is the tab's own title, not a section label inside it: the tab's name
		      lives in a tooltip now that the rail is icon-only, so this is the only place the
		      page says what it is. It used to carry the roll-mode pill on its own line as well,
		      which is what the hand-written markup was originally for. --}}
		<h3 class="stonetop-move-group-title">{{localize "stonetop.steading.tabs.moves"}}
			{{> "stonetop.section-collapse" collapse="steadingMoves"}}
		</h3>
		<ol class="items-list">
			{{#each stonetop.moves}}
			<li class="stonetop-item steading-move-card{{#unless rollable}}{{#unless interactive}} move-unowned{{/unless}}{{/unless}}">
				<div class="stonetop-item-header">
					{{> "stonetop.steading-move-controls"}}
					<strong class="stonetop-item-name stonetop-steading-move-open">{{label}}</strong>
				</div>
				{{#if description}}<div class="stonetop-item-description">{{{boldMissText description}}}</div>{{/if}}
			</li>
			{{/each}}
		</ol>
	</div>

	</section>
</div>
